# Text files are LF in the repository and in every working tree, whatever core.autocrlf says: the
# tests read their inputs byte for byte (the .pure corpus: parser parity is byte-exact; the generated
# files, each diff-tested against its generator; the goldens). Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would check them out as CRLF; eol=lf keeps them LF, and text=auto still
# normalizes a CRLF saved by an editor to LF on commit. Binary files are detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

